From: Tao Gong <gongtao0607@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: mt7530: trap frames to conduit in MFC on EN7581 and AN7583

On EN7581, frames trapped by the switch (BPDUs, and link-local frames such
as LLDP) only reach the CPU when MT7530_CPU_EN and MT7530_CPU_PORT are also
set in MT753X_MFC.

Like MT7531 and MT7988, EN7581 and AN7583 only set the CPU port bitmap in
MT7531_CFC and are skipped by mt753x_conduit_state_change(). On EN7581 this
is not enough, so trapped LLDP frames never reach the conduit interface and
LLDP neighbours behind switch user ports are never seen.

Add EN7581 and AN7583 to mt753x_conduit_state_change() so the MFC CPU port
bits are programmed as well.

Tested on AN7581: with this change, LLDP frames from a device on a switch
user port are delivered to lldpd; without it, they are dropped.

Fixes: 2b0229f67932 ("net: dsa: mt7530: Add EN7581 support")
Signed-off-by: Tao Gong <gongtao0607@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c
@@ -3274,8 +3274,9 @@
 	 * forwarded to the numerically smallest CPU port whose conduit
 	 * interface is up.
 	 */
-	if (priv->id != ID_MT7530 && priv->id != ID_MT7621 &&
-	    priv->id != ID_EN7528)
+	if (priv->id != ID_MT7530 && priv->id != ID_MT7621 &&
+	    priv->id != ID_EN7528 && priv->id != ID_EN7581 &&
+	    priv->id != ID_AN7583)
 		return;
 
 	mask = BIT(cpu_dp->index);
